# Security Onion SOC Lab

## Objective

This project demonstrates how to simulate network attacks and detect them using Security Onion in a monitored laboratory environment.

## Lab Architecture

![Architecture](screenshots/security onion architecture.png)

Machines used in this laboratory:

- Kali Linux : attacker machine
- Ubuntu : target machine
- Security Onion : network monitoring and intrusion detection platform

## Attack Simulation

The attacker machine generated ICMP traffic using the ping command.

Command executed on Kali Linux:

ping 192.168.1.16

## Traffic Capture

Network packets were captured and saved in a PCAP file.

Example command:

tcpdump -i eth0 -w capture.pcap

This command records network packets into the file **capture.pcap**.

## Intrusion Detection

Security Onion analyzed the captured network traffic using IDS tools such as Suricata and Zeek.

The system detected suspicious ICMP traffic generated by the attacker machine.

## Alerts

Security Onion generated alerts that were visible in the SOC dashboard.

Screenshots of these alerts are available in the **screenshots** folder.

